#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105541 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105870 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b6c58537-344e-5842-b68c-d9b5a9d7ca96" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Triangle"}] :question/id #uuid "fc5fc31e-f585-5d15-8a8a-eb0d19704e9a" :question/math-academy-id "e-2947" :question/problem "Find the area of the triangle $\\triangle ABC.$\n\n![](images/f8/f892cd084f548769fa6b7352fece0e1aef3a66a4ab517ed5b5243d89041ac3a9.png)" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{A} = \\dfrac{b \\cdot h}{2},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $b$ is a base and $h$ is the corresponding height.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the base is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =AB \\\\  & =AH+HB \\\\  & =6+3 \\\\  & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the corresponding height is\n\n$$\nh={CH} = 4 .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\cdot 4}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{2} \\\\  & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105542 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105871 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6445834c-7788-5427-a72c-30b06cc8e6ab" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of an Isosceles Right Triangle"}] :question/id #uuid "cdb1d145-6e8a-5213-a7f7-8076440cbbeb" :question/math-academy-id "e-2949" :question/problem "What is the area of the right triangle $ABC$ shown below?\n\n![](images/3b/3b68fc0b5c128122e7316db08e34932393db5bf557ffd889fd785265b758b447.png)" :question/worked-solution "Since $m\\angle{A}=m\\angle{C},$ we have an isosceles triangle, where $AB=BC.$\n\nTherefore, the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AB\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 8\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {8}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 64 \\\\  & =32.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105543 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105872 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7656d23-06c9-5d22-b62a-3636bca66ab6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Base or the Height of a Triangle Given Its Area"}] :question/id #uuid "58e1ce31-f6fc-5900-ab89-e00241045b12" :question/math-academy-id "e-2950" :question/problem "Consider the triangles $\\triangle ABC$ and $\\triangle CDE$ shown below. If the area of $\\triangle CDE$ is $25 \\textrm{ cm}^2,$ find the area of $\\triangle ABC.$\n\n![](images/bd/bd9840fd674fe7bf7b4f428591dfc6e9fbbaec8387836ece34694d17eaabe65b.png)" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider $\\triangle CDE.$ We can see that $\\overline{CD}$ is the height corresponding to the base $\\overline{DE}$ and that $DE=10\\textrm{ cm}.$ \n\nSince the area of $\\triangle CDE$ is $25\\textrm{ cm}^2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2} \\\\ 25 & =\\frac{10\\cdot CD}{2} \\\\ 25 & =5\\cdot CD \\\\ CD & =5\\text{ cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that $\\overline{CD}$ is also the height of $\\triangle ABC$ corresponding to the base $\\overline{AB}.$\n\n![](images/ea/ea7f44b91e87a42029c5f00aae97a2eebf2e472ff890d4b91f4973e1e383e5c7.png)\n\nTherefore, we find the area of $\\triangle ABC$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{AB\\cdot CD}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\cdot 5}{2} \\\\  & =15{\\text{ cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354593 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105871 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6445834c-7788-5427-a72c-30b06cc8e6ab" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of an Isosceles Right Triangle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01a966f4-dbc7-5e7f-b5c3-6801e6e0fd63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351579} {:answer/id #uuid "078fe28f-b6f9-59e7-baa7-6f94535bdc55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351633} {:answer/id #uuid "1ce73c74-b0aa-5831-857d-258578d42122" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351825} {:answer/id #uuid "43cc795c-8aa7-515c-bcc6-e9198bafacc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352189} {:answer/id #uuid "67484ca0-9ae4-56cc-8e1f-cda96489e093" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352485}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67484ca0-9ae4-56cc-8e1f-cda96489e093" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352485} :answer-field/id #uuid "acc38aa9-2f81-50eb-be6b-41072cd0d10e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354120}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b779fa51-4da1-5c93-b91d-35c3acfc0806" :question/math-academy-id "q-87801" :question/problem "![](images/f1/f18be4b42008423fe08b165fea4b3807b247813112b92a6ad0932c07a33ba8b6.png)\n\nWhat is the area of the right triangle $ABC$ shown above?" :question/worked-solution "Since $m∠A=m∠C$, we have an isosceles triangle, where $AB=BC.$\n\nHence, the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AB\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {4}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 16 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354594 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105871 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6445834c-7788-5427-a72c-30b06cc8e6ab" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of an Isosceles Right Triangle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0663bea7-12f5-5928-84d7-bc207c70bfaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351623} {:answer/id #uuid "3101c5fb-53ba-5942-ad43-1ae35079f738" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352018} {:answer/id #uuid "7e914068-1f39-55f3-a988-748244647a92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "200" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352677} {:answer/id #uuid "8150fcea-b946-540d-b0fd-6ae56c257637" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352692} {:answer/id #uuid "aa336a88-ddef-5077-bcae-4e7bf818c424" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353009}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3101c5fb-53ba-5942-ad43-1ae35079f738" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352018} :answer-field/id #uuid "69982ee7-0741-5c08-835f-b26951ee678f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354013}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "298d5629-725b-5aa5-9d76-4ed61398d66b" :question/math-academy-id "q-87802" :question/problem "![](images/37/3756b00cce29aad77b7a0b1ebb09f43cb89a602f8462edce89e8ba6346cb7fab.png)\n\nWhat is the area of the right triangle $ABC$ shown above?" :question/worked-solution "Since $m∠A=m∠B$, we have an isosceles triangle, where $AC=BC.$\n\nHence, the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {10}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 100 \\\\  & =50.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
